{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that","id":758474,"title":"I like to play Uber Conservative Chars, is Ragabash incompatible with that?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-06T05:53:38-08:00","id":758474,"title":"I like to play Uber Conservative Chars, is Ragabash incompatible with that?","content":"I like to play chars who are deeply conservative , treat Metis as abominations, kinfolk as perpetual children and helpers, even as property...<br /> <br /> Decidedly classist, sneering at bone gnawers.../<br /> <br /> a trace of misogyny is optional.<br /> <br /> Is all that incompatible with Ragabash?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-06-2015, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T06:29:46-08:00","id":758528,"title":"","content":"Well, it's not likely, but it's not impossible. One could be a racist bastard ragabash to lampshade the xenophobia of the Garou and show it as a sham. Also, you could be a Ragabash who is of the quiet, sneky, stabby type rather then the questioner type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T06:33:20-08:00","id":758535,"title":"","content":"Maybe some silver fang who doesn't get out much &quot;you're a plumber? What on Gaia is that?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T06:56:17-08:00","id":758591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that#post758474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to play chars who are deeply conservative , treat Metis as abominations, kinfolk as perpetual children and helpers, even as property...<br /> <br /> Decidedly classist, sneering at bone gnawers.../<br /> <br /> a trace of misogyny is optional.<br /> <br /> Is all that incompatible with Ragabash?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Why would it be? You get to preach the uncomfortable truth that Metis Deformities are a liability in combat. You get to point out how important Kinfolk are for Garou survival...and how utterly useless they are for all the Garou stuff. You get to point out every time the weak softhearted liberal modern crybabies in the Sept fuck things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:12:28-08:00","id":758610,"title":"","content":"Well, since Ragabash are considered, even tasked with testing out wether or not any practise holds true or should be abolished, you may have an interesting opportunity there.<br /> Most see the Ragabash as testing the old rules (and rightly so), but they have to test the NEW ones too, maybe even more so.<br /> If you`d like to play a traditionalist, all you have to do is focus your suspicion and &quot;testing of the rules&quot; on all the new and liberal rules younger Garou are so eager to introduce into the sept.<br /> Metis are a valuable part of the comunity? Well lets see if that holds true under pressure then...<br /> It would be a controversial character concept in our eyes (as players, not as characters), but no less valid. I actually imagine there to be quite a number of this kind of Ragabashs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:13:26-08:00","id":758612,"title":"","content":"I agree with etherial above. I can absolutely see that being compatible. Hopefully you'll have a mature Troupe to play with that will realise the characters views dont necessarily reflect your own and they'll give the Ragabash plenty of opportunity to teach and highlight what is both wrong and right, good and bad, favourable and distasteful, a crutch and a strength, natural to garou but preferable to humanity and problems that could, do and might arise.<br /> <br /> Certainly should create food for thought. Unless the chatacter is just doing it to be an ass <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but it could certainly have potential for some interesting situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:22:57-08:00","id":758622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=758610#post758610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, since Ragabash are considered, even tasked with testing out wether or not any practise holds true or should be abolished, you may have an interesting opportunity there.<br /> Most see the Ragabash as testing the old rules (and rightly so), but they have to test the NEW ones too, maybe even more so.<br /> If you`d like to play a traditionalist, all you have to do is focus your suspicion and &quot;testing of the rules&quot; on all the new and liberal rules younger Garou are so eager to introduce into the sept.<br /> Metis are a valuable part of the comunity? Well lets see if that holds true under pressure then...<br /> It would be a controversial character concept in our eyes (as players, not as characters), but no less valid. I actually imagine there to be quite a number of this kind of Ragabashs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this interpretation. Testing of new rules is something that doesn't get considered enough among the Garou. Mind you, I'd still be careful, since...<br /> <br /> a) Metis can and will tear your head off for being a dick to them<br /> b) kinfolk have it hard enough without a ragabash riding them for kicks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:25:16-08:00","id":758625,"title":"","content":"I also agree with Seki above. Good points well made. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:27:58-08:00","id":758630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=758622#post758622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like this interpretation. Testing of new rules is something that doesn't get considered enough among the Garou. Mind you, I'd still be careful, since...<br /> <br /> a) Metis can and will tear your head off for being a dick to them<br /> b) kinfolk have it hard enough without a ragabash riding them for kicks</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it all depends on the tribe. Fenrir/Walker/Gnawer/CoGGie/Strider/Fury metis? Sure. But the rest would still face some sort of punishment for it.<br /> <br /> As for kinfolk, they can't really complain to anyone about it. Especially if its ragabash just doing their job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T09:23:57-08:00","id":758883,"title":"","content":"Considering the position of kinfolk in Garou society, what valuable lessons do you offer if you treat them like garbage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T09:27:38-08:00","id":758891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=758630#post758630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for kinfolk, they can't really complain to anyone about it. Especially if its ragabash just doing their job.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can dig their heels in and refuse to help though. And the Elders will probably grow annoyed pretty quickly with any ragabash that starts dismantling their kinfolk support network with their tedious bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T09:27:52-08:00","id":758892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=758622#post758622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like this interpretation. Testing of new rules is something that doesn't get considered enough among the Garou. Mind you, I'd still be careful, since...<br /> <br /> a) Metis can and will tear your head off for being a dick to them<br /> b) kinfolk have it hard enough without a ragabash riding them for kicks</div> </div> </div> </div>[Ultraconservative Ragabash]<br /> a) If they <i>try</i>, you have all the proof you need. As soon as the metis swings, his life is forfeit.<br /> b) All the more reason to keep them in their place. It's only when they get out of their place that trouble happens.<br /> [/Ultraconservative Ragabash]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T09:54:45-08:00","id":758917,"title":"","content":"Just to help<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=758883#post758883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the position of kinfolk in Garou society, what valuable lessons do you offer if you treat them like garbage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody said this. <br /> <br /> It was &quot;..how important Kinfolk are for Garou survival...and how utterly useless they are for all the Garou stuff. &quot;<br /> <br /> Which is quite different. <br /> <br /> Also Kinfolk could complain. I dont imagine many other of their relatives and friends would be happy if they were treated poorly and I'd like to think if anyone did get too upset it wouldnt be long till a Garou confronted the True in question over their loved one. Grievance Challenges happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T10:52:28-08:00","id":759031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=758892#post758892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [Ultraconservative Ragabash]<br /> a) If they <i>try</i>, you have all the proof you need. As soon as the metis swings, his life is forfeit.<br /> b) All the more reason to keep them in their place. It's only when they get out of their place that trouble happens.<br /> [/Ultraconservative Ragabash]</div> </div> </div> </div>How does a) compute? There is nothing that stops Garou beating the crap out of each other outside a rep hit, and the metis will be getting more than enough rep hits in such an environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T10:57:55-08:00","id":759044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=759031#post759031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does a) compute? There is nothing that stops Garou beating the crap out of each other outside a rep hit, and the metis will be getting more than enough rep hits in such an environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because any action a metis takes in tribes that would do that is watched. They are assumed to be shit, and among the Fianna for example, Wyrm tainted. Therefore, if a Fianna metis attacks a ragabash, it is clearly a sign that the metis is tainted. Or just overstepping its bound. Therefore, it needs to be punished.<br /> <br /> Some garou can even hold beliefs that the metis was allowed to live on probation, and acting outside its station means it has used up that good will.<br /> <br /> Freaking disturbing, yeah. But it happens in tribes that hate metis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T11:20:23-08:00","id":759079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=759044#post759044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because any action a metis takes in tribes that would do that is watched. They are assumed to be shit, and among the Fianna for example, Wyrm tainted. Therefore, if a Fianna metis attacks a ragabash, it is clearly a sign that the metis is tainted. Or just overstepping its bound. Therefore, it needs to be punished.<br /> <br /> Some garou can even hold beliefs that the metis was allowed to live on probation, and acting outside its station means it has used up that good will.<br /> <br /> Freaking disturbing, yeah. But it happens in tribes that hate metis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this quite jives. Being a Metis doesn't mean that others are always right and you are always wrong. Metis are second class, but they are still Garou. I think even in the most dickish tribes, they realize that Metis have value (especially in the face of the impending Apocalypse). Metis aren't to be kicked and spit on, they are twisted warriors to be goaded and used as weapons against Gaia's enemies.<br /> <br /> Addendum: I do not really see the point of playing a character that acts out the worst stereotypes of the Garou Nation. These prejudices exist, but collecting them all into a single character just sounds really really dumb and basically an excuse to act out a jerk fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-06-2015, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T11:26:05-08:00","id":759081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=759079#post759079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think this quite jives. Being a Metis doesn't mean that others are always right and you are always wrong. Metis are second class, but they are still Garou. I think even in the most dickish tribes, they realize that Metis have value (especially in the face of the impending Apocalypse). Metis aren't to be kicked and spit on, they are twisted warriors to be goaded and used as weapons against Gaia's enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on the sept and tribe. To use Fianna as an example (again), a metis was not allowed to join a pack without a lot of effort in the revised tribebook. As well, the book details a lot just how utterly the Fianna do not want any of their metis to ever rise high.<br /> <br /> I should note that, for MOST of the Nation, you are right. It's tribes like Wendigo and Fianna that are so extreme, generally. Or just some random sept somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:57:12-08:00","id":759211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=759079#post759079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think this quite jives. Being a Metis doesn't mean that others are always right and you are always wrong. Metis are second class, but they are still Garou. I think even in the most dickish tribes, they realize that Metis have value (especially in the face of the impending Apocalypse). Metis aren't to be kicked and spit on, they are twisted warriors to be goaded and used as weapons against Gaia's enemies.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Being a Metis means you have to have a thick skin. A Ragabash's job is to test that. If you can't handle yourself in the Sept, how are you supposed to resist the predations of the Wyrm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T13:18:43-08:00","id":759243,"title":"","content":"Nothing I've read says that a Ragabash like this can't exist. There may be social consequences for his actions, but then again an overprotective Child of Gaia could also face consequences for coddling weakness in the untested (i.e. Metis, Kin, and maybe the younger wolves).<br /> <br /> That answered, what Tribe are you intending. I think the focus has been too much on the question of Metis' role in society, which may have influenced the suggestions of Fianna and Uktena earlier. A Silver Fang could also work, as could a Get of Fenris (in the MET system, their tribal weakness had them become intolerant of one thing they considered a weakness). That said, do you have an idea what tribe you were going to go as for this character, and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T14:41:03-08:00","id":759363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=759211#post759211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a Metis means you have to have a thick skin. A Ragabash's job is to test that. If you can't handle yourself in the Sept, how are you supposed to resist the predations of the Wyrm?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like we aren't talking about quite the same thing. If the Garou are taking swipes at each other, physical ones are as good as literal ones. The Ragabash says something dumb/clever, the Metis smacks him upside the head, if she can catch him. If the Ragabash says something dumb/clever and the Metis <i>frenzies,</i> you are completely right and she should get whatever is coming to her.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-06-2015, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T16:13:40-08:00","id":759471,"title":"","content":"One of the keys to being a good Ragabash is knowing your limits and not doing things that will get you fucked up. There is no special shield for the Ragabashes being assholes just because they are Ragabash. This is something very important to remember when you go around playing Mr. Asshole. A good Ragaash is one that causes chaos and does not end up a victim to the consequences of his tricks. A bad Ragabash quickly collects enemies, battle scars, punishment rites and renown losses. Note that the Ragabash is supposed to be the contrarian, and that most septs will be conservative, so being a Ragabash who is pro conservatism is missing the point. You go from being the challenger to being the supporter of the status quo. Heck you go to being Troll for the status quo.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, I'm quite willing to agree that the lot of a Metis is a harsh one, and that they have a hard time in their society, however, it should be stressed that Garou are rare and that their society is based on meritocracy. The rarity itself means that you will want to keep the metis around at least as long as possible to be an effective combatant. The meritocracy means that once they earn their recognition, it's a hard time to actually keep them down without a systemic abuse and backstabbing behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> There are smaller septs who are quite against metis, who hate the mere fact that they exist, but most such septs will not be keeping such Garou, they are likelier to kill them or toss them out to fend for themselves then to actually keep them. The Litany tenet on not tending to anyone's sickness can easily be twisted into this. Why would they waste effort and resources on such a creature? Just to use them as punching bags?<br /> <br /> If it somehow does conspire that a metis in such a sept grows up, or has the misfortune of a large sept that can spare some resources on getting him up to being cannon fodder, why does that metis stay? What does he have to gain? Let's say that he is a whipped weakling and that he has been turned into a self fulfilled prophecy, he is the punching bag for the sept as is. Why would that sept need a Ragabash to mock him and show how bad he is? Where is the renown in getting a victim to suffer further? Who rewards it? Why? And while I could get a NPC sept that exists to showcase the evils of xenophobia, I'm deeply disturbed by the idea of players that seek to play this kind of character.<br /> <br /> In a sept that is more oriented towards integrating the metis (Even if just they need more bodies), the Ragabash pushing this party line will not have universal support for his attitude. He will be in the right to challenge the status quo, and his philosophy might get traction if he can actually get the other Garou to learn something from it. However, if he just picks on the metis or the kinfolk without actually having a point, he will end up losing renown and making himself into a troublemaker that might even be worse then the metis. At least the metis know their place and don't kick a fuss... this guy just drags them out into the spotlight with his crap. And no one wants the metis to be in the spotlight. This might mean that he actually helps the Metis of the Caern with his atitude.<br /> <br /> In a sept where the metis are treated as mostly equals, I can see the biggest benefit of a contrarian. He runs the risk of being sanctioned by his superiors, but he may have actual wisdom to impart, and when he actually proves a lesson, he will be raking in renown for showing them that while they may not be wrong to embrace the metis, that there are risks and problems that can be prevented by actually thinking why the metis in the past have been a problem.<br /> <br /> These same thoughts apply to the kinfolk issue as well. The extreme of that argument ends with kinfolk breeding camps to churn out new Garou, and that's not only missing the point of kinfolk, but truly and utterly horrible and beyond anything the Garou would ever do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T16:26:56-08:00","id":759488,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to say I fully support the idea you have for your character Prince of the Night. Dont let anyone tell you how to play it, in the end the only thing you can regret is not playing it how you artistically conjured it and brought into creation. Happy gaming in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> &quot;In a society as traditional and conservative as that of the Garou Nation, a free-thinking individual with the right to speak his or her mind is absolutely important, whether to encourage change or to reaffirm the current position through the challenges he or she provides.&quot;<br /> <br /> Freethinking. Go for it and enjoy no moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:19:06-08:00","id":759555,"title":"","content":"LOL Cogliostro... remember in book of auspices a gift that DID in fact act as a shield to a ragabash no matter how rude he was as long as he was HONEST","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:56:49-08:00","id":759582,"title":"","content":"Actually read the wording. It's not about covering rudeness, it's about covering you stating uncomfortable facts to people that do not want to hear them, as long as they are the Truth as adjudicated by the ST (and Cat... this looks like Chicanery-No way before Chicanery-No <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). It's also pretty hard to pull off multiple times on the same target in a row. And it still isn't a sure shot since the target can use Willpower to shrug it off if you really, really pissed them off.<br /> <br /> It's also notable as a Level Three Gift, which is something that's awarded to experienced Ragabash who have had to earn quite a bit of renown by actually surviving all the crap they pulled.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T18:20:44-08:00","id":759605,"title":"","content":"No, it's not incompatible. Go for it. It's a piss poor Ragabash that can only &quot;question&quot; things by adhering to some (for a Garou) left wing stereotype agenda.<br /> <br /> Odysseus is probably a good example of a Ragabash character in real myth that has trickster like traits, but is essentially on the side of the powers that be. He is the complete henchman of Agamemnon that does all the dirty work, uses guile to get people to do the things he wants them to do, and deceive the enemy.<br /> <br /> If you really want to be a &quot;questioner of the ways&quot;, there are all sorts of ways to do so. After all, in past times when all Garou treated metis like crap, demeaned kinfolk, etc., Ragabash probably weren't all 21st century Western liberals. They found other ways to question the Garou.<br /> <br /> The entire point of the &quot;questioner of the ways&quot; isn't too undermine the Litany or Garou society. It's too make sure their thinking doesn't get so hidebound that they are tricked by their enemies or are unable to adapt.<br /> <br /> An easy way to be a &quot;conservative&quot; Garou is to take the &quot;liberal&quot; talking points and bring them to their logical, but absurd, conclusion:<br /> <br /> 1) Is the sept being too nice to the Metis? Well, they obviously know better than Gaia since she cursed them. What else do they think she did wrong?<br /> 2) Is the sept too accepting of kinfolk as equal? Well, maybe it's time for them to stop being slackers and do all the things the Garou do. Which of course will get them killed and therefore useless to the nation.<br /> 3) Is the sept too welcoming of bone gnawers? Well, maybe more tribes should be like them - not keep track of their kinfolk, accept criminals and lazy to boost their numbers, care so little of the Litany they engage in cannibalism, etc. Oh, those are actually bad things? Then why are we not holding the Bone Gnawers to the same standards we hold ourselves?<br /> <br /> Democracy and egalitarianism has its bad side too - mob rule, lowering of standards, undermining of traditional morality, etc. - just like hierarchical society does.<br /> <br /> After all, hasn't the adoption of these modern liberal ideas been the same time the Wyrm has grown in power? Is it just coincidence? Isn't it possible - just possible, it is these ideas that allow evil to flourish in the name of &quot;tolerance&quot;?<br /> <br /> If you want more ammo for such a view, do an internet search on the &quot;dark enlightenment&quot;. You'll learn a lot of how &quot;neo-reactionaries&quot; think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T19:23:50-08:00","id":759644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=759079#post759079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Addendum: I do not really see the point of playing a character that acts out the worst stereotypes of the Garou Nation. These prejudices exist, but collecting them all into a single character just sounds really really dumb and basically an excuse to act out a jerk fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it all depends on the exact game and what game style and characters concepts fits with the other players and ST. It could be very disruptive to the game, or not. It's possible to play &quot;jerk&quot; characters and still have everyone at the table have fun. I think it is even possible to play a very &quot;conservative&quot; Garou and not have it be done as a jerk or a caricature. Flawed or intolerant characters could have virtues as well, and such characters can be very fun and interesting to play and be played with.<br /> <br /> I do agree that it could lead to trouble with the other players or the ST depending on what they want to see. Always best to discuss character concepts with the group so everyone can see why their own character wants to be in the same pack as the other PCs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T00:06:06-08:00","id":759789,"title":"","content":"I would say being Radically Regressive is a role the Ragabash take in society(I wouldn't call it conservative per se as they actively push things in a different direction, vs merely fighting to maintain the status quo). The question is more what you expect out of said character and if the ST understands this. I'd be prone to hit him with &quot;very special episodes&quot; and getting hit hard for having these sorts of flaws.(Metis dies gloriously defending your fox frenzy, treating Kinfolk like shit leads to a skindancer etc) so you'd have to be very clear with the ST what you want out of playing this character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T00:11:08-08:00","id":759794,"title":"","content":"So maybe something like a Stephen Colbert type character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T03:41:59-08:00","id":759867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=759644#post759644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it all depends on the exact game and what game style and characters concepts fits with the other players and ST. It could be very disruptive to the game, or not. It's possible to play &quot;jerk&quot; characters and still have everyone at the table have fun. I think it is even possible to play a very &quot;conservative&quot; Garou and not have it be done as a jerk or a caricature. Flawed or intolerant characters could have virtues as well, and such characters can be very fun and interesting to play and be played with.<br /> <br /> I do agree that it could lead to trouble with the other players or the ST depending on what they want to see. Always best to discuss character concepts with the group so everyone can see why their own character wants to be in the same pack as the other PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Point is because I played in a lot of the worse VTT Games on AOL Over a decade ago... ran into WAY too many Uber liberal garou... to the point where my Char was treated as if she might as well be a card carrying KKK member, for referencing a Metis derisively as a 'mule'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T04:03:29-08:00","id":759876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that#post758474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to play chars who are deeply conservative , treat Metis as abominations, kinfolk as perpetual children and helpers, even as property...<br /> <br /> Decidedly classist, sneering at bone gnawers.../<br /> <br /> a trace of misogyny is optional.<br /> <br /> Is all that incompatible with Ragabash?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really , there are plenty of ragabash in the fianna. And they are basically that.....plus drinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T05:38:19-08:00","id":759917,"title":"","content":"Know about their treatment of Metis... but are you sure on the other things? Am PLAYING a homid Fianna ragabash in wyld west right now, as fate would have it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T07:47:24-08:00","id":759981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=759867#post759867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Point is because I played in a lot of the worse VTT Games on AOL Over a decade ago... ran into WAY too many Uber liberal garou... to the point where my Char was treated as if she might as well be a card carrying KKK member, for referencing a Metis derisively as a 'mule'</div> </div> </div> </div>Online games and LARPs have their own dynamic different from tabletop. What I noticed from them is that every character is the unique snowflake and exception to the settings, so it makes the game a mess from a canonical perspective. A tabletop game can handle a player or even the entire PC group being &quot;different&quot; since the ST can be sure to make the rest of the chronicle consistent with the setting - your Camarilla game looks like a Camarilla game, your Garou act like Garou.<br /> <br /> In those games, I've often played the &quot;jerk&quot; character, and I've found the other players really liked that because I was one of the few characters in the game they wanted to play off because I was one of the few who played a character consistent with the setting. In essence, you are in much more of an ST running a single NPC than a PC. One part of doing this is to not just be a jerk, but to be jerk in ways that is conducive to others having fun. That's not always easy to pull off.<br /> <br /> I don't know your situation a decade ago, but I'm sure some of those characters treating you badly probably had players who were very glad that character was there. However, there are those who are living vicariously through their characters and working out their own issues who may take offense. There's nothing you can do about that - these kind of huge online games are not a proper forum for therapy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T08:47:09-08:00","id":760006,"title":"","content":"Yes ... I would have understood a tenative &quot;Perhaps we should re examine our ways&quot; Not the &quot;What is wrong with you?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T09:00:13-08:00","id":760013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=759917#post759917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Know about their treatment of Metis... but are you sure on the other things? Am PLAYING a homid Fianna ragabash in wyld west right now, as fate would have it...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the werewolf game i have played being a fianna was carte blanche to be dismissive/predjudiced against people with disabilities, homophobic, obviously hating the metis, treating kinfolk as property. Hell we had bad guy in there that was fianna ragabash that kidnaped a kinfolk because it was his &quot;property&quot; and put her in a potato sack. So it kinda fits.<br /> <br /> While the Silver Fangs are all of that also there is difference in that at their best the SFs can be, very rarely are but can be, the heroic tribe they sell themselves as while the fianna at their best they are drunk frat boys aimed at people you dont like but maybe thats whats their revised tribebook sold me.<br /> <br /> However, thats not to say its a bad character to play as <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\">Black Fox</a></b> pointed out playing the asshole is not bad, it can be a very interesting and in a way a counter point for the more typical political correct PCs but also dont get surprise when someone puts a silver bullet in your character`s back of the neck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-07-2015, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T09:25:58-08:00","id":760029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=759981#post759981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Online games and LARPs have their own dynamic different from tabletop. What I noticed from them is that every character is the unique snowflake and exception to the settings, so it makes the game a mess from a canonical perspective. A tabletop game can handle a player or even the entire PC group being &quot;different&quot; since the ST can be sure to make the rest of the chronicle consistent with the setting - your Camarilla game looks like a Camarilla game, your Garou act like Garou.<br /> <br /> In those games, I've often played the &quot;jerk&quot; character, and I've found the other players really liked that because I was one of the few characters in the game they wanted to play off because I was one of the few who played a character consistent with the setting. In essence, you are in much more of an ST running a single NPC than a PC. One part of doing this is to not just be a jerk, but to be jerk in ways that is conducive to others having fun. That's not always easy to pull off.<br /> <br /> I don't know your situation a decade ago, but I'm sure some of those characters treating you badly probably had players who were very glad that character was there. However, there are those who are living vicariously through their characters and working out their own issues who may take offense. There's nothing you can do about that - these kind of huge online games are not a proper forum for therapy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much this. As someone who is solely a forum/online gamer, I -loved- when we got a traditional garou character in the game. And I always played a metis.<br /> <br /> Though, I must admit that when I started, the playing field was -really- bad. Only city games, no lupus allowed. It made the games into a huge mess of Walkers and Gnawers AND VERY liberal Silver Fangs. Also, auspice roles outside philodox, ahroun and theurge were not always respected.<br /> <br /> I've played some jerk characters, myself. I think the mentality to them is to offer an antagonist for the others to face, and understand it. That way, you have a lot of fun, and others can have the settings elements enforced smartly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T10:30:17-08:00","id":760064,"title":"","content":"When can a character who makes people question their values be extremely conservative? When he's surrounded by liberals of course. Sure, a Get of Fenris Ragabash might try to get his brethren to see that violence isn't always the answer and maybe that a physically weak pack mate can be useful and should be respected. But what about a Child of Gaia Ragabash, maybe they need to remind their pack that there need to be some limits on tolerance and acceptance, that the old laws and prejudices exist for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T10:35:27-08:00","id":760067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=760029#post760029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very much this. As someone who is solely a forum/online gamer, I -loved- when we got a traditional garou character in the game. And I always played a metis.<br /> <br /> Though, I must admit that when I started, the playing field was -really- bad. Only city games, no lupus allowed. It made the games into a huge mess of Walkers and Gnawers AND VERY liberal Silver Fangs. Also, auspice roles outside philodox, ahroun and theurge were not always respected.<br /> <br /> I've played some jerk characters, myself. I think the mentality to them is to offer an antagonist for the others to face, and understand it. That way, you have a lot of fun, and others can have the settings elements enforced smartly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there should be fair balance, i have played pbp games which the DMs were hardasses pushing everyone to play stereotypes because that whole &quot;i want my werewolf/camarilla/changeling game to look like werewolf/camarilla/changeling game&quot; bullshit.<br /> <br /> With things like &quot;yeah your fenrir has to be a racist&quot; even though said character had no contact with the fenrir in his life. Or even ignoring parts of the settings like the renewalist camp in the SFs just to push an stetic choice for a game instead of showing that through npcs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T11:00:15-08:00","id":760080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=760067#post760067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think there should be fair balance, i have played pbp games which the DMs were hardasses pushing everyone to play stereotypes because that whole &quot;i want my werewolf/camarilla/changeling game to look like werewolf/camarilla/changeling game&quot; bullshit.<br /> <br /> With things like &quot;yeah your fenrir has to be a racist&quot; even though said character had no contact with the fenrir in his life. Or even ignoring parts of the settings like the renewalist camp in the SFs just to push an stetic choice for a game instead of showing that through npcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously. I think the DMs should give a setting and somewhat watch the concepts, but let the players have free hands otherwise. A lot of the best RP has come from different characters and their viewpoints.<br /> <br /> ...I swear it is always Fenrir and racism that shows the issue. It's like the sign you need to run, if you see a ST saying all Fenrir are racists by default. Or, mention the mixed-heritage flaw for them.<br /> <br /> But yes, a huge deal has been made to make the game 'accurate' in a lot of places. And often, it fails utterly. I tend to treat each game as its own universe for that reason.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I should note I have absolutely no problem with induvidual characters being racists. Two characters others played that I considered good have been nao-nazi. It's the whole 'ALL of the Fenrir are racists' that is the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 11-07-2015, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T16:21:05-08:00","id":760318,"title":"","content":"noted this elsewhere... but while I am comfortable with Fascist PC's I dont like the Swords of Heimdall not entirely sure why... when I LIKE Chars who treat kin like property, Metis as bastards etc...and am usualy ok with the red talons genocidal agenda...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T16:30:55-08:00","id":760327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=760318#post760318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">noted this elsewhere... but while I am comfortable with Fascist PC's I dont like the Swords of Heimdall not entirely sure why... when I LIKE Chars who treat kin like property, Metis as bastards etc...and am usualy ok with the red talons genocidal agenda...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sad thing is, that when its assumed, its not just one of the camps. It's the -entire- tribe. Somehow, 2nd ed Fenrir tb just keeps truckin' over later canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"