nyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T16:29:55-08:00","id":827151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=826975#post826975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, one thing to remember, is that the character pushing things needs a bit of standing before pushing too hard. A Black Fury Ahroun may treat her husband as a punching bag/sex toy, ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Husband?<br /> <br /> I don't think such radical feminist would have one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3673-mu_","name":"Mu_","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3673_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:08:55-08:00","id":827174,"title":"","content":"Arise necro thread arise!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T17:09:08-08:00","id":827175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mu_</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=827151#post827151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Husband?<br /> <br /> I don't think such radical feminist would have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cannot tell if serious...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T23:06:41-08:00","id":827334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mu_</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=827151#post827151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Husband?<br /> <br /> I don't think such radical feminist would have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, please be a bad joke post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T07:16:28-08:00","id":827493,"title":"","content":"Maybe there is something I am losing because English is not my native tongue, but I am not talking about reasonable feminism. Ok, this is not even feminism. I don't think a Black Fury should treat men as punching bag/sex toy, but if there would be one, I don't think she would marry one. It does not make sense to feel so superior to men so you think you can abuse them that way, but joining one in marriage. I know that in the opposite way happens sometimes, but this is in the context of the patriarchal system.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I am sorry to getting so out of topic, but that grabbed my attention a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3673-mu_","name":"Mu_","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3673_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T09:25:46-08:00","id":827566,"title":"","content":"I find a very conservative Ragabsh makes a great concept. For it is a often underestimated facet of the ragabash to also show the rest of pack/sept, when they are unnecessarily or dangerously liberal or untraditional. By putting their behaviour to the extreme, and acting really, really untraditional, a ragabash should/could/would remind everyone, that there is a tradition to adhere to and why it is important.<br /> <br /> It works best for lupus and metis ragabash, and for traditional tribes better than for the liberal ones, but I find the general idea of pointing out the flaws in any given plan is great for any ragabash, even if the flaw is just, that the planned action is not traditional (enough).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T14:16:24-08:00","id":827779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/758474-i-like-to-play-uber-conservative-chars-is-ragabash-incompatible-with-that?p=827566#post827566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find a very conservative Ragabsh makes a great concept. For it is a often underestimated facet of the ragabash to also show the rest of pack/sept, when they are unnecessarily or dangerously liberal or untraditional. By putting their behaviour to the extreme, and acting really, really untraditional, a ragabash should/could/would remind everyone, that there is a tradition to adhere to and why it is important.<br /> <br /> It works best for lupus and metis ragabash, and for traditional tribes better than for the liberal ones, but I find the general idea of pointing out the flaws in any given plan is great for any ragabash, even if the flaw is just, that the planned action is not traditional (enough).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly it mostly makes sense for player packs, since players will tend towards being the least conservative of all Garou","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}